From 06261765a554228678f08f13915ea5df6811eb1e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 12:37:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] Wire cohort equity findings into live judgment (mortgage
 only, ACTION_FLAG)

Closes the per-decision wiring gap left open in cohort-assembly and
lending-cassette (fetch_latest_cohort_review existed as a read but was
never called from the live path). Wm's decision, 2026-07-31: escalate
for human review, never touch the automated score.

RegulatoryDeck gains optional twin_client/replica_id constructor args --
both required together, default None (off). When configured, judge()/
explain() check whether the domain cassette being judged declares
CAPABILITY_OUTCOME_OBLIGATION and, if so, fetch the most recent
cohort_equity_review for that decision's (domain, obligation_kind). A
FLAGGED review produces one c2_cohort_equity_rollup finding per live lens
exposing c2_rollup -- always ACTION_FLAG, never ACTION_BLOCK, so the
deck's existing 'findings ride NEXT TO the judgment' guarantee keeps the
score untouched and judgment never blocks on this. explain() surfaces the
same finding read-only, same posture as cross-lens-tier-conflict
detection -- no disclosure write.

Domain-agnostic by design (any future cassette enabling
outcome_obligation gets this for free), but only mortgage exercises it
today -- it is the only cassette declaring CAPABILITY_OUTCOME_OBLIGATION,
per Wm's request to note that explicitly.

A twin fetch failure (unreachable, unauthorized, etc.) is caught and
treated as 'no review recorded yet' -- fails OPEN, so a twin-connectivity
problem degrades this one optional signal, never live judgment itself.

9 new tests in test_regulatory_cassettes.py (disabled-by-default,
capability gating, no-review-yet, clean-review-no-op, flagged-review
escalates with score untouched, never blocks, disclosed once to the
ledger, appears in explain() without writing, fails open when
unauthorized). Full suite 689 passed / 6 skipped, twice back-to-back.
Ruff and bandit clean on every touched file (bandit's only findings
anywhere in the touched test files are pre-existing B101/B608 baseline
noise, confirmed via git stash diff against main).
